WEBVTT

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:47.520
Everyone! The matchups for the tournament have been decided!

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:48.000
One more time!

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.370
Here it is, here it is! Seishuu...

00:01:54.370 --> 00:01:56.940
So... who're we playing first?

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:59.420
Y-Youka High School?

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:02.150
What is it? Are they strong?

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:08.440
All right! This'll be easy!

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.380
They're a weak team that usually loses in the second game!

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:13.850
Are you serious? Great!

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:17.360
The people we're going up against after that, Mifune, are seeded,

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:18.830
but they're not all that famous.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:23.240
At the look of things, we might be able to get pretty far!

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:24.750
Let's go then!

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:27.550
We'll show Kanagawa how strong Seishuu is!

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:29.900
Yeah! Let's do it!

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:33.380
They're forgetting that they're beginners and are getting all cocky.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:35.010
S-Shimizu-kun!

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:37.000
We're lucky.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.310
Now, even if we put Shigeno on reserve, we'll be able to win.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:43.730
Who're you putting on reserve?

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:48.760
Shigeno!?

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:50.950
Geez...

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:53.090
Stop joking around.

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:55.520
If the ace isn't here, the game can't start.

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:57.410
Hey, don't overdo it.

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:01.080
You should recover slowly and get back into your best condition before pitching.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:07.010
I told you... say that kind of stuff <i>after</i> you see my pitches.

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:26.200
<i>This past week I've been working hard to rebuild my lower body.</i>

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:29.940
<i>There're only two weeks until the tournament.</i>

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:31.780
<i>I don't have any more excuses!</i>

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:37.330
<i>All right!</i>

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:44.880
That was amazing, Shigeno!

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:48.150
The speed and the break, it's the same as before!

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:51.720
Were you really injured, you bastard?

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:54.440
Didn't I tell you?

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:57.290
What do you think I'm doing rehab for?

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:03.490
<i>I guess I forced myself too much with the running.</i>

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:08.300
Nogoro-kun. I have to talk to you.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.690
Please come with me. 

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:12.880
Oh, and Shimizu-kun, you too.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:22.540
W-What? It's not me but Taiga who's the starting pitcher?

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:23.680
That's right.

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:26.000
So, Shimizu-kun, 

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.380
please prepare yourself for the game.

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:30.030
Okay...

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:31.550
Hold on a second! 

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:34.340
Didn't I say I've already recovered?

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.340
I wonder about that.

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:38.510
I just went to the hospital to check on things,

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:43.310
and it seems as though you haven't been to your checkups lately.

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:47.300
Yeah. What about it?

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.270
If there aren't any problems, there's no need to go, right?

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:55.310
Then please go now and get a doctor's note.

00:04:55.920 --> 00:05:00.230
If the doctor okays it, I'll let you be the starting pitcher.

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:02.290
It doesn't have anything to do with you!

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:05.880
Don't worry about my body!

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:06.960
It's a pain.

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:09.460
Don't flatter yourself.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:13.430
No one is worried about you.

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:15.590
It's just that, as the advisor,

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:20.640
I can't do something as irresponsible as leaving the team's fate in the hands of an injured player.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:23.990
The baseball team is not your property.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:25.180
Even if you aren't here,

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:29.080
everyone on the team can still fight with their heads held high, isn't that right?

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:33.250
I see. 

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:35.820
So he <i>was</i> pushing it.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:38.830
Well, I guess there's nothing we can do.

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:42.970
If he's not healed, he won't be able to pitch properly.

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:53.820
Goro!

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:55.380
How long are you going to sleep till?

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:57.330
You have a game at 9:30am, don't you?

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:59.020
You won't make it in time!

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:05.100
Be quiet.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:08.360
I don't <i>have</i> to make it, 

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:10.810
since I won't be able to pitch.

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:17.770
W-Wait, Goro! What are you talking about?

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:22.490
Coming!

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:33.410
I knew you'd do something like this. 

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:36.300
By the coach's orders, we came to get you.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:38.010
W-What!?

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:39.970
Well then, Shigeno-kun?

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:56.930
What do you want?

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:59.100
You'll do fine without me, right?

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:04.050
If you put a guy like me on the bench now, the team's morale will just be lowered.

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:06.080
Yes. 

00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:07.910
That's why...

00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:11.040
I wasn't planning on forcing you to sit on the bench.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:15.750
But... they were the ones who wanted you to.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:22.550
"Even if he can't play in the game, we still need him,

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:27.700
because the Seishuu baseball team is a team formed by Shigeno Goro.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:32.440
If he wants to pitch, let him pitch.

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:34.730
Even if we lose because of it,

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:39.940
both he and we won't regret anything."

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:51.370
I'll leave everything to you.

00:07:52.680 --> 00:08:01.920
Take your injury and the team into consideration. It's your own responsibility to decide whether to pitch or not.

00:08:03.150 --> 00:08:06.370
Because this is <i>your</i> tournament.

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:12.100
Let's have a good game!

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:28.780
You're fine with this, right, Nogoro-kun?

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:30.450
Yeah.

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:33.660
If I can't trust them even during the first game,

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:36.250
we won't be able to persevere and play against Kaido.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:41.980
Tateishi-kun, what's the data on that pitcher?

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:45.190
There is no game data.

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:48.940
He's a first-year who used to play shortstop for the Yokohama Seniors.

00:08:49.930 --> 00:08:54.390
A first-year; they're using a first-time pitcher on a newly established baseball team?

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:58.860
It seems we might get a few chances to score.

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:02.270
Play ball.

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:04.890
All right! Get your spirits up!

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:07.080
First, win the first game!

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:14.850
Strike! Batter out!

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:17.120
His curve ball is good.

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:19.170
Is he really a first-year?

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:23.090
Strike! Batter out!

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:27.300
All right! All right!

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:29.600
Out!

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:31.190
Three outs, change!

00:09:31.190 --> 00:09:32.640
All right!

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:33.080
Okay! Okay!

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:34.560
Nice pitching, Taiga!

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:36.170
You rascal!

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:38.960
This is your first time up on the mound and you're not even nervous.

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:40.620
You're quite a guy.

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:43.280
Nervous? What's that?

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:49.450
What was that? 

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:51.210
That was their fastball?

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:54.580
Kaido's pitcher was way faster, wasn't he?

00:09:56.230 --> 00:09:58.220
We've won this game!

00:09:58.220 --> 00:10:00.630
Even if Shigeno's not in the game, it'll be an easy win!

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:07.630
All right! Nice, Taiga!

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:11.850
Batting second: third baseman, Uchiyama-kun.

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:14.750
Nogoro-kun.

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:18.060
Uchiyama-kun is waiting for your signal.

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:21.270
Didn't I say I'd leave everything up to you?

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:24.080
Right now, Seishuu's coach... is you.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:25.230
Right now, Seishuu's coach... is you.

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:48.420
Out!

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:53.100
Batting third: catcher, Tashiro-kun.

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:53.100
Nice bunt.

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:01.770
All right!

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:09.650
They're better than I thought.

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:13.370
Out!

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:15.330
Out!

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:16.830
Three outs, change!

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:20.090
Damn, right in front?

00:11:20.090 --> 00:11:21.840
That was close, wasn't it, Fuji?

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:23.920
It was a good hit too.

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:25.390
But if it keeps going like this,

00:11:25.390 --> 00:11:26.800
we'll be able to score runs whenever we want!

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:30.350
We might even win by the mercy rule!

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:33.150
Well then...

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:35.890
Tashiro.

00:11:35.890 --> 00:11:38.670
I'm leaving the rest to you.

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:40.530
I'm going to go move my body.

00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:44.230
If you're up against these guys,
you should be able to handle them.

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:48.690
I have to start training to be able to do what I can for the next game.

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:50.840
But, Nogoro-kun...

00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:52.630
All right! Go, go!

00:11:52.630 --> 00:11:53.950
Everyone, you're fine with it, right?

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:55.700
Yeah.

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:59.220
Somehow, our confidence has gone up since we went up against Kaido's second string.

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:02.160
And I'm not as nervous as I thought I would be.

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:04.880
I guess there's no problem.

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:10.080
However, we might win by the mercy rule, so make sure you get back early!

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:15.760
You have to stay in the stadium.

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:17.090
Yeah.

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:19.080
See ya later.

00:12:22.230 --> 00:12:23.630
Let's go!

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:25.210
YEAH!

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:29.000
Now then,

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:30.900
time to make our comeback.

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:35.910
This is a free fansub.

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:35.910
Not for sale or rent.

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:41.660
<i>Lower your shoulders and hit it towards the ground.</i>

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:43.810
<i>It doesn't matter if it's right in front of the fielders.</i>

00:12:43.810 --> 00:12:46.210
<i>They're a team of amateurs.</i>

00:12:52.050 --> 00:12:53.340
All right! 

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:53.760
Huh?

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:57.430
<i>An opening will definitely appear somewhere.</i>

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:00.580
What's that idiot doing?

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:01.930
Don't mind! Don't mind!

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:05.380
Hey, what are you doing?

00:13:05.890 --> 00:13:09.610
S-Shut up! Come again!

00:13:10.250 --> 00:13:13.030
Batting fifth: shortstop, Yokoi-kun.

00:13:13.030 --> 00:13:14.110
Geez...

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:22.060
Safe!

00:13:26.810 --> 00:13:30.800
<i>It seems as though this is the first time he's pitched with runners on base.</i>

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:36.780
To first!

00:13:38.030 --> 00:13:38.970
Out!

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:45.770
Out!

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:48.730
Safe!

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:51.650
No way... They've caught up.

00:13:51.650 --> 00:13:55.710
B-But... it's not as if they got hits. 

00:13:56.530 --> 00:13:59.600
Batting fifth: first baseman, Miyazaki-kun.

00:13:59.600 --> 00:14:01.000
Hit it, Miyazaki!

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:03.450
Score as many runs as you can!

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:05.730
He seems determined to get a hit.

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:09.420
Yes... we don't need strikes against such players.

00:14:14.340 --> 00:14:14.840
Out!

00:14:23.570 --> 00:14:24.180
Out!

00:14:26.810 --> 00:14:28.100
Out!

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:34.580
Ball! Four balls!

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:39.320
Damn it!

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:42.780
Suzuki-san...

00:14:43.470 --> 00:14:44.990
I have a favor to ask you.

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:49.010
I'm late after all!

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:52.170
Hey, Shimizu!

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:52.170
Oh, Honda!

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:55.670
Honda?

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:57.090
What is it?

00:14:57.650 --> 00:14:59.240
What do you mean, "what is it"?

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:01.440
What're you doing out here?

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:03.020
Isn't it the middle of the game?

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:08.000
Can't you tell? I'm leaving the game to them and I'm training.

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:11.850
Shigeno-senpai!

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:17.070
Please come back to the bench quickly!

00:15:23.490 --> 00:15:26.510
It's the seventh inning and it's 8-1!?

00:15:29.580 --> 00:15:33.250
It's a better result than we thought it would be, isn't it, Coach?

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:34.900
Well, of course.

00:15:34.900 --> 00:15:41.010
Our players may be ordinary, but everyone has been working hard for more than two years with this summer in mind. 

00:15:41.010 --> 00:15:45.470
We won't lose to a high school team that's never entered a tournament before.

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:49.810
How many runs for the mercy rule?

00:15:49.810 --> 00:15:53.050
At least a seven run difference by the end of the seventh inning.

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:56.020
Then... if we don't get any runs this inning...

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:57.480
it'll be a mercy game.

00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:59.860
How did this happen?

00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:01.650
There's no other reason.

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:05.700
Everyone's falling over each other's legs...

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:09.920
I was an idiot to dream for an instant that we could get to Koshien with a team like this.

00:16:09.920 --> 00:16:11.120
What'd you say?

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:12.920
Show me that.

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:14.690
W-What do you want?

00:16:15.330 --> 00:16:18.390
They began with a safety bunt and a walk,

00:16:18.390 --> 00:16:21.200
and then a squeeze and a sacrifice fly to score three runs.

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:24.870
With our errors, five runs?

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:27.350
Didn't they only have three hits?

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:29.470
It's like playground baseball.

00:16:29.470 --> 00:16:30.990
You little brat!

00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:34.020
This entire game you've been talking big and complaining the entire time!

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:35.120
The fielders have been defending and-

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:35.980
Fuji!

00:16:35.980 --> 00:16:38.650
It's not the time to be arguing about that!

00:16:41.210 --> 00:16:41.860
Out!

00:16:43.130 --> 00:16:44.730
Only two outs left...

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:47.320
Batting first: pitcher, Shimizu-kun.

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:49.990
My turn, huh?

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:52.780
Get on base somehow, Taiga!

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:57.170
Just one run! If you can score one run,
we'll be able to do something about it later.

00:16:57.170 --> 00:16:59.580
Are you being serious?

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:04.050
This team doesn't have the ability to get those seven runs back.

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:09.010
Well, I'll try and hit a big one.

00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:18.960
Go away.

00:17:18.960 --> 00:17:22.360
We don't need someone who doesn't have the will to fight until the very end. 

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:27.050
The batter is changing to number 10.

00:17:26.300 --> 00:17:27.870
That guy... is his leg okay?

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:38.050
<i>This player... His form and attitude are good.</i>

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:41.550
<i>He seems a bit different from the other players.</i>

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:44.720
Strike!

00:17:45.810 --> 00:17:47.430
<i>Stop joking around.</i>

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:51.430
<i>How can I lose at a place like this!?</i>

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:55.600
Go out!

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:01.150
That idiot!

00:18:01.150 --> 00:18:03.070
Don't force yourself with that leg of yours!

00:18:09.220 --> 00:18:10.440
Safe!

00:18:11.010 --> 00:18:12.060
He did it!

00:18:12.060 --> 00:18:13.160
But what about his leg?

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:22.040
Senpai!

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:24.600
Is your leg okay?

00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:28.300
I ran <i>because</i> it was okay, didn't I?

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:33.260
Instead of worrying about me, you guys just need to think about winning.

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:35.930
Winning?

00:18:35.930 --> 00:18:39.140
Batting second: third baseman, Uchiyama-kun.

00:18:40.350 --> 00:18:43.730
A seven run difference and he goes all-out with an injury, huh?

00:18:44.650 --> 00:18:46.450
How unfair. 

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:49.260
Because of a passionate guy like him,

00:18:49.260 --> 00:18:51.620
he makes me, who's being realistic, seem like the devil.

00:18:51.620 --> 00:18:52.710
You bastard!

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:53.930
What is it?

00:18:53.930 --> 00:18:58.070
You guys don't think that you can make a comeback too, right?

00:18:58.070 --> 00:19:04.130
Isn't your actual goal to score a run this inning so you don't lose by the mercy rule?

00:19:04.590 --> 00:19:07.920
Against a team that's tougher than expected...

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:10.920
And it's the first official game in front of a crowd.

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:10.340
Strike!

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:15.470
Nervousness, uncertainty, insecurity, carelessness.

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:17.450
After coming this far,

00:19:17.450 --> 00:19:21.350
the fact that you have very little experience, haven't practiced enough, and have poor skills,

00:19:21.350 --> 00:19:23.730
everyone's noticed that, haven't they?

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:29.900
That was pretty impressive made-up commentary.

00:19:30.280 --> 00:19:32.920
You don't think that Honda can make a comeback?

00:19:34.250 --> 00:19:35.410
Ball!

00:19:36.550 --> 00:19:37.590
Safe!

00:19:37.590 --> 00:19:39.700
Don't say stupid things. He's serious.

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:42.420
He's seriously planning on making a comeback.

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:46.170
Even now, when we're losing by seven runs...

00:19:46.170 --> 00:19:48.330
Are you an idiot?

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:51.520
When he can't even stand on the mound because of his injury,

00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:54.930
how's he planning on winning with a team of amateurs?

00:19:56.150 --> 00:19:57.640
He's going to affect the others.

00:19:59.150 --> 00:20:04.310
His fighting spirit is going to affect the people around him to the point that it's unbelievable.

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:10.900
All right!

00:20:12.780 --> 00:20:14.600
We've gotten past the mercy rule!

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:16.630
Keep going, Tashiro!

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:17.700
All right!

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:21.420
Shigeno! The way that you're walking...

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:25.240
Just concentrate on hitting a fastball, Tashiro.

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:28.380
The pitcher is getting tired, and he can't throw change-ups anymore.

00:20:28.380 --> 00:20:29.710
O-Okay.

00:20:29.710 --> 00:20:30.960
O-Okay.

00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:32.930
<i>Affect others?</i>

00:20:39.980 --> 00:20:41.900
Ball! Four balls!

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:44.230
It's one out and the bases are loaded!

00:20:44.910 --> 00:20:48.730
What do you mean, "affect others"? It's just a bunch of luck.

00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:56.330
Pitcher, replacing Tsugimura-kun: Hiranaka-kun.

00:20:58.060 --> 00:20:58.700
What?

00:21:01.090 --> 00:21:02.730
Sidearm, huh?

00:21:02.730 --> 00:21:05.750
Just when we were finally getting used to that pitcher.

00:21:08.850 --> 00:21:10.730
<i>You're pretty good, old man.</i>

00:21:10.730 --> 00:21:15.520
<i>Even though they have the lead, he noticed our boost in morale and took action immediately.</i>

00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:24.060
Strike!

00:21:24.060 --> 00:21:25.260
<i>G-Give me a break!</i>

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:27.290
<i>G-Give me a break!</i>

00:21:27.290 --> 00:21:30.270
<i>I'm so afraid of these kinds of situations...</i>

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:32.680
<i>I can't hit it...</i>

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:36.240
<i>I won't be able to hit it at all, and I'll end up dampening everyone's spirit.</i>

00:21:38.490 --> 00:21:40.550
Strike!

00:21:40.550 --> 00:21:41.890
<i>See?</i>

00:21:41.890 --> 00:21:44.750
<i>There's no way a beginner can hit those pitches based on morale alone.</i>

00:21:45.250 --> 00:21:48.210
Miyazaki! Straighten your back!

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:51.670
Don't get scared! Keep your head up and hit it!

00:21:51.670 --> 00:21:58.050
Were you practicing that hard for half a year to take those cowardly swings?

00:21:58.980 --> 00:22:00.600
<i>That's right...</i>

00:22:01.080 --> 00:22:02.780
<i>I've practiced as well.</i>

00:22:03.780 --> 00:22:05.610
<i>I was bad at sports...</i>

00:22:06.300 --> 00:22:08.280
<i>but I practiced! </i>

00:22:09.560 --> 00:22:11.230
<i>Even I...</i>

00:22:19.570 --> 00:22:20.450
Second!

00:22:22.980 --> 00:22:23.910
Safe!

00:22:28.450 --> 00:22:29.290
Safe!

00:22:29.670 --> 00:22:30.950
All right!

00:22:30.950 --> 00:22:32.250
Great job, Miyazaki!

00:22:34.460 --> 00:22:36.470
<i>Y-You're kidding me...</i>

00:22:36.470 --> 00:22:39.640
<i>I did a Guts-Pose without even thinking.</i>

00:22:42.130 --> 00:22:43.350
All right! A double play!{Is this timed right, or a missing tl?}

00:22:44.810 --> 00:22:46.840
Run five!

00:22:45.470 --> 00:22:48.180
Yay! Only three runs left!

00:22:48.180 --> 00:22:49.690
We can do it!

00:22:52.820 --> 00:22:54.600
We aren't very lucky, are we?

00:22:54.600 --> 00:22:58.570
No, luck won't come to those who have thrown all hope away.

00:22:59.040 --> 00:23:02.030
They've called luck to themselves.

00:23:02.620 --> 00:23:08.750
But the ones to laugh last will be our team. 

00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:43.180
Switching with Taiga, I get up on the mound.

00:24:43.610 --> 00:24:47.390
Now that this has happened, I don't care whether my leg hurts!

00:24:47.390 --> 00:24:51.480
But the other team's coach has noticed my injury.

00:24:52.430 --> 00:24:53.790
Next time, on Major: 

00:24:53.790 --> 00:24:55.060
Wounded Ace.

00:24:55.060 --> 00:24:57.500
Run to the stage of your dreams!
